  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-fix-cursor-dao/seek-duplicates-null-from-last",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-CURSOR-1",
    "D-CURSOR-1",
    "CUR-SEEK"
  ],
  "description": "Repairs r-cursor-1/seek-duplicates: Seek \"=\", Null on IX_K began on ID 6, which is already the first row of IX_K (Null sorts first), so the landing could not be told from a Seek that did not move. Table D has K values 1,2,2,2,3,Null for IDs 1-6. For IX_K and for IX_KN (WITH IGNORE NULL) in turn: a fresh table-type recordset over D, Index set, MoveLast, read ID and K (the start); Seek \"=\", Null; read Errors, NoMatch, BOF, EOF, ID and K; MoveNext and read ID; MovePrevious and read ID; on IX_KN then MoveFirst and walk ID to EOF (at most 16); close. Asks where a Null key lands on an index that holds nulls and on one that ignores them, starting from a row that is not the first. The fixture copy is opened read-only.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
